        "original_id": "4287fc4e-21c5-5ed1-99ec-e4f6f4c94875",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ian Hunter, Rob Thomas\n- Bands: Mott the Hoople, Matchbox 20\n- Albums: Dirty Laundry\n- Roles: lead singer, singer-songwriter, record producer, multi-instrumentalist\n\nFacts:\n- Ian Hunter Patterson was born on 3 June 1939 and is known professionally as Ian Hunter.\n- Ian Hunter is a British singer-songwriter.\n- In 1969, Ian Hunter became the lead singer of the English rock band Mott the Hoople at the band's inception.\n- Mott the Hoople dissolved in 1974 after Ian Hunter had served as its lead singer from 1969.\n- In 2009, Ian Hunter returned as lead singer for a Mott the Hoople reunion.\n- In 2013, Ian Hunter again served as lead singer for a Mott the Hoople reunion.\n- Dirty Laundry is the eighth solo album by Ian Hunter.\n- Robert Kelly Thomas was born on February 14, 1972.\n- Rob Thomas is an American singer, songwriter, record producer, and multi-instrumentalist.\n- Rob Thomas is best known as the lead singer of the alternative band Matchbox 20.",
